From: Jarkko Sakkinen <jarkko.sakkinen@opinsys.fi>
Subject: [PATCH] block: mark devices without media unavailable

An empty removable-media device can return ENOMEDIUM when DiskBusy opens
it exclusively. Propagating that error aborts ListDisks, hiding usable
target drives as well.

Treat missing media as a per-device unavailable reason. The TUI can keep
listing other disks, while installation-time validation still rejects the
empty device. Other open errors continue to propagate.

--- a/src/engine/block.cc
+++ b/src/engine/block.cc
@@ -287,6 +287,8 @@ std::string_view BusyReasonText(BusyReason reason) {
       return "swap";
     case BusyReason::kInUse:
       return "in use";
+    case BusyReason::kNoMedia:
+      return "no medium";
   }
   return "in use";
 }
@@ -403,6 +405,9 @@ StatusOr<std::optional<BusyReason>> DiskBusy(const std::filesystem::path& drive,
     if (error == EBUSY) {
       return BusyReason::kInUse;
     }
+    if (error == ENOMEDIUM) {
+      return BusyReason::kNoMedia;
+    }
     return ErrnoToStatus(error,
                          fmt::format("open {} exclusively", devnode.string()));
   }
--- a/src/engine/block.h
+++ b/src/engine/block.h
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ enum class BusyReason : std::uint8_t {
   kRaid,
   kSwap,
   kInUse,
+  kNoMedia,
 };
 
 std::string_view BusyReasonText(BusyReason reason);
